{"model":"typesafe/jev-1.14","state":{"message":"A few conventions I need you to follow across this repository, because two incidents came from skipping them.

Before any schema change lands, run the migration suite against a scratch database and paste the result. Keep the rollout commit separate from the code commit, so a reviewer can revert one without the other. If a test is flaky, fix or delete it in the same pull request instead of rerunning the pipeline until it goes green.

That last one matters more than it sounds: the rerun habit hid a broken index for six weeks, and I would rather see a red pipeline than a second version of that.","activeAnchor":null,"activeItems":[]},"questions":{"kind":{"type":"choice","instructions":"What kind of instruction is the user's message? Judge only the message, not the items.","criteria":{"objective":"States the overall goal of the whole session or project","sub-goal":"Assigns a concrete deliverable or task that should be tracked until it is done","rule":"A standing instruction for all later work: always, never, prefer, conventions","decision":"Picks or confirms one option among alternatives, a choice that should not be reopened","steering":"A correction or direction that only applies to the work currently in progress","ephemeral":"Anything else: questions, one-off action requests, acknowledgements, status chatter, pasted content"}}}}

{"model":"typesafe/jev-1.14","state":{"message":"We spent the last two days comparing the two cache options and I want to close that out.

Option A was SQLite on the local volume: one file, trivial backup, but the write contention under the replay test pushed p99 to 480 ms. Option B was PostgreSQL with a small connection pool: one more service to run, p99 at 90 ms on the same corpus.

